i.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105285","id":2797576089,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mv5-Z","user":{"login":"monitz87","id":7144213,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDQyMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7144213?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87","html_url":"https://github.com/monitz87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T17:27:36Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T17:27:36Z","body":"I don't see anything wrong with the use case I laid out. In fact, it's a very common usage and there is *NO* way to work around it for plugin developers unless you explicitly instruct all the plugin users to not use typed dictionaries at all when using your plugin.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797576089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797612033","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105285#issuecomment-2797612033","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105285","id":2797612033,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mwCwB","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T17:35:29Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T17:42:36Z","body":"I'd say in this case the code *is* wrong if the dictionary is expected to accept `String` as key, but it's not at all impossible to work around, just use the key information to check if it's typed, in this case I'd say there's lacking type safety and type checks in your code, the switch statement also is dependent on the `__type` entry being a `String`\n\nIt would also be confusing unless this also changes the `get` method","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797612033/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797632589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105285#issuecomment-2797632589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105285","id":2797632589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mwHxN","user":{"login":"monitz87","id":7144213,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDQyMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7144213?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87","html_url":"https://github.com/monitz87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T17:46:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T17:46:00Z","body":"This is a very hot code path. Having extra checks is expensive. The whole reason for the key having a preceding double underscore is that it is meant for internal use. Users of the plugin wouldn't create dictionaries with a `__type` key, so there shouldn't be a risk of it being mistyped. And it's much more reasonable to add a usage instruction to not use a specific key than telling them to avoid typed dictionaries.\n\nAs for `get`, IMO it should also be changed. The point of `get` is to try to fetch a key safely even if you don't know whether it is there or what it contains.\n\nBoth `has` and `get` seem dynamic enough that they shouldn't care about type safety.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797632589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"per